  {
   "title": "Inequality: more than, not as … as",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "h",
     "t": "1. A is better than B"
    },
    {
     "type": "pattern",
     "title": "A + lalóng (or higít na or mas) + adjective + káysa kay (or káysa sa) + B",
     "rows": [
      {
       "label": "Example",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "Si Peter",
         "r": "noun"
        },
        {
         "t": "ay",
         "r": "ay"
        },
        {
         "t": "lalóng",
         "r": "other"
        },
        {
         "t": "marúnong",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "káysa",
         "r": "other"
        },
        {
         "t": "kay",
         "r": "marker"
        },
        {
         "t": "John",
         "r": "noun"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "note": "Peter is brighter than John."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "The first noun is usually the one with **more** of the quality. **Lalóng** (laló + the ligature -ng), **higít na** (higít + the ligature na) and **mas** all mean *more*; **káysa** means *than*."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Like the possessive words ni and ng (Lesson 8), **káysa kay** is followed by the name of a person, while **káysa sa** is followed by the name of a place or thing. **Káysa sa** may be shortened to **kesa**."
    },
    {
